<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Antiochus IV Epiphanes</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Antiochus IV</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Antiochus IV Epiphanes was a Seleucid king who reigned from 175 to 164 BCE. He invaded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> but was forced by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> to withdraw. His attempts to impose Hellenistic religious practice in Judea provoked the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maccabean-revolt">Maccabean Revolt</a>, which contributed to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seleucid-empire">Seleucid Empire</a>'s loss of territory and is commemorated in the festival of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hanukkah">Hanukkah</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/antiochus-iv-epiphanes.jpg" alt="Antiochus IV Epiphanes" width="280" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: José Luiz · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Antiochus_IV_Epiphanes_-_Altes_Museum_-_Berlin_-_Germany_2017.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
